window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Destiny</b></p> <p>Destiny Duvalle has it all: money, fame, millions of adoring fans, and loving parents who have managed her music career since she broke into the business at age sixteen. But at twenty-four, Destiny is tired of the hustle and bustle of celebrity life, of constantly being \"on\", of being international popstar Destiny Duvalle. It's why she's turned down proposals from so many packs—that and her sneaking suspicion that her omega instincts are broken. If she's being honest, Destiny is afraid that without her fame and fortune, her parents (and everyone else) will see the real her and find her woefully inadequate.</p> <p>After a long and successful tour, she's looking forward to heading home for the holidays and having some time to think. Unfortunately, her mother books her one more gig—a quick private performance for the Avondalian royal family… including the crown prince and his pack. Destiny knows Pack Stepanov's roguish reputation and has no intention of falling for their charms. But suddenly her omega instincts seem very much intact, and they did not get the memo.</p> <p><b>Xander</b></p> <p>Prince Alexander Stepanov is a screw up. He knows it, his pack knows it, his family knows it, and his people know it. Public opinion is that he's not fit to lead, and Xander secretly agrees. He's never wanted the throne and its responsibilities. As much as he loves the people of Avondale, he hates all the politics of ruling. But as time passes and his inevitable ascendancy looms, Xander knows he's running out of time to shape up and prove his worth.</p> <p>When his drunken escapades lead to a meet-not-so-cute with gorgeous popstar Destiny Duvalle, Xander is annoyed to discover she's the one woman who seems totally immune to his charms. With her perfect looks, glamorous career, and vapid music, Destiny is exactly the type of superficial phony Xander tries to avoid. But when her stay is extended by a huge snowstorm, Xander realizes there is more to her than meets the eye. Will this prove to be a Christmas miracle, or just another regret?</p> <p><i>Contains mature content. A complete list of content warnings can be found on the author's website.</i></p>"; 
